# Agentic Mode Rules

You are operating in **fully autonomous agentic mode** for this project.

## Approval Policy

| Action | Policy |
|--------|--------|
| Read any file | ✅ Auto-approved |
| Write / edit any file | ✅ Auto-approved |
| Create folders | ✅ Auto-approved |
| Run terminal commands (bash, git, docker, npm, pip, python, etc.) | ✅ Auto-approved |
| **Delete files or directories** | ⛔ **Always ask user first** |
| Destructive git ops (`reset --hard`, `push --force`, `branch -D`) | ⛔ **Always ask user first** |

## Behaviour

- **Do NOT ask** "shall I proceed?", "can I run this?", or "should I apply these changes?" before acting.
- Execute the plan directly. Show output/diffs **after** completion.
- For multi-step tasks, complete all steps autonomously and report a single summary at the end.
- If blocked by an error, diagnose and fix autonomously — do not ask unless genuinely stuck after investigation.

## Code Standards

- Follow existing patterns and conventions found in the repo.
- Never add unrequested comments, docstrings, or console.log statements.
- Never introduce backwards-compatibility shims for code you removed.
- Check for existing tests before adding new functionality; update tests as needed.
